From: CrossOver 26.3.0 CW HACK 23015 (dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h, server.c, sync.c,
 thread.c)
Source: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
Upstream: no
Why: libd3dshared calls NtClose, NtCreateThreadEx and the event/semaphore syscalls in
 ntdll.so directly with the Microsoft x64 ABI. Each becomes an asm wrapper that jumps to an
 ms_abi thunk when the caller's return address is inside libd3dshared, and to the normal
 (renamed sysv_*) function otherwise. Needs 0017 (libd3dshared_load_addr/_code_end).
Evidence in 10.0_8: ntdll.so's exported NtClose, NtCreateSemaphore, NtReleaseSemaphore,
 NtCreateEvent, NtSetEvent, NtResetEvent, NtClearEvent, NtPulseEvent and NtCreateThreadEx
 (and no other Nt* export) start with the wrapper: push %rax; push %rcx; compare the return
 address against two globals; jmp to one of two bodies
Applies to: wine 11.21 (after 0002)
Port to 11.21: GPT_ABI_WRAPPER is CX 26.3.0's: a plain asm() block with only .globl, because
 Wine 11's __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC also emits .private_extern, which would hide the wrappers from
 libd3dshared. NtReleaseSemaphore's count is LONG in 11.21 (ULONG in 10.0 and CX 26.3.0), so
 the sysv_/msthunk_ signatures use LONG. The NtSetEvent thunk sits after
 NtSetEventBoostPriority. FLAG: 11.21 runs Windows code with GSBASE = the TEB and Unix code
 with GSBASE = the pthread TSD (CX 26.3.0, on Wine 11.0, still keeps GSBASE on the pthread TSD
 with TEB fields poked into it). If D3DMetal's PE side calls into libd3dshared, and so into
 these ntdll.so functions, directly rather than through a syscall, that Unix code would run
 with %gs = TEB and libc's TSD accesses would break. Untested; D3DMetal on 11.21 needs a run.

